    "The interpretation of rising probe AUC as 'strengthening answer pre-commitment = latent unfaithfulness' needs careful defense in the paper. A model could have high probe AUC AND high causal reliance if it uses CoT to verify pre-committed answers. The joint NLDD measurement addresses this, but the framing in the description conflates predictive power with unfaithfulness.",
    "Moderate-high scoop risk persists: the Obfuscation Atlas team (FAR AI, who have 500+ trained RLVR models on HuggingFace and existing probe infrastructure) and the pre-CoT probe team (Cox et al.) could independently converge on this study. The compressed 6-8 week timeline helps but doesn't eliminate this risk.",
    "The 'LLMs Encode How Difficult Problems Are' paper (2510.18147) already demonstrates the methodology of training linear probes at GRPO checkpoints (on Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B) — while their focus is difficulty encoding rather than faithfulness, this should be cited as a methodological precedent and further reduces methodological novelty.",
